 "notes": "E371 duplicates the unit's own row; its basin and cisterns are recorded once (own row, position none). Other E/S duplicates (E360, E363, E359) recorded once. N31 ('Aqaba, Tell el- (Cypros), 12 m) is a separate Nigro point; its cisterns and pool take grid N31. SWP Beit Jubr et Tahtani matches Nigro N36; its birkeh 'immediately south of the fort' takes grid N36. SWP Tell es Sultan entry: only section 6 (Tellul Abu el 'Aleik, S2539, 1.1 km) is within 2 km; its 'rectangular chamber' is a room, not coded; Tell es Sultan/'Ain es Sultan features and Warren's mound graves near 'Ain es Sultan are beyond 2 km; text cut at 12,000 characters. Kypros basin has no size: pool_def unclear. N7 pits (2nd century AD) coded U. Rock shelters, niches, cliff not coded. No explicit absence statements."
